# Project Context

This repository is the **Respondi backend**: an AWS CDK application written in TypeScript. It uses one stack per environment (`RespondiBeStack-development`, `RespondiBeStack-staging`, `RespondiBeStack-production`), Lambda + API Gateway for HTTP, and Cognito for auth.

- **Lambdas:** `src/lambdas/` — path-based layout (e.g. `auth/signup/post/`). One handler per folder; each `index.ts` exports `handler`. Shared code lives in `src/lambdas/utils/` and is copied into each handler bundle at build time.
- **Infrastructure:** CDK entry in `bin/respondi-be.ts`. Constructs live in `bin/lib/`. Keep a single stack. Add new routes on the Rest API in that stack.
- **Layers:** Extra npm libraries that are not in the Node.js 22 runtime go in the node-modules layer (`scripts/build-node-modules-layer.js`, `bin/lib/node-modules-layer.ts`). `@aws-sdk/*` stays external.
- **Build:** `npm run build:all` compiles handlers into `dist/lambdas` and installs the layer into `dist/layers/node-modules`. CDK deploys those artifacts.
- **Database:** Not chosen yet. Do not add RDS, DynamoDB, or Prisma until the store is decided.
- **Auth:** Cognito email/password plus Google ID-token sign-in. Account identity currently lives on the Cognito user (`custom:authProvider`, `custom:providerSubject`).

Do not add Express, Fastify, or any other HTTP server framework. All APIs are served only via API Gateway and Lambda.
